  "helpTitle": "Quick guide",
  "tourWelcomeTitle": "Welcome to TrailBuddy",
  "tourWelcomeText": "This is where the trails you have ridden live, and those of your buddies — nobody else’s. Three ways bring trails here: import a GPX, record a ride, connect with buddies.",
  "tourWelcomeStart": "Start the tour",
  "tourMapIntroTitle": "The map",
  "tourMapIntroText": "Your trails and your buddies’ trails live here, each line in the color of its difficulty. The tour shows what the map tells you — and what is behind the buttons.",
  "tourMapNavTitle": "The sections below",
  "tourMapNavText": "Trails: all of them as a list, search and filter. Buddies: who sees your trails — and you theirs. Profile: import, rides, areas and the quick guide.",
  "tourMapBadgeTitle": "The sign at the start",
  "tourMapBadgeText": "Every trail starts with its sign showing grade and character; the dot below points its arrow in the riding direction. A tap on the sign — or on the line — selects the trail, a second one opens its sheet.",
  "tourMapSheetTitle": "The trail sheet",
  "tourMapSheetText": "Length, elevation and the difficulty as your network sees it — a tap on the grade shows who rated it how.",
  "tourMapColorsTitle": "Color means difficulty",
  "tourMapColorsText": "Every line carries its trail’s difficulty like a ski run. The style of the line tells its condition: crumbly means worn, dashed means beaten up, faded means barely rideable. An orange edge means a report, a yellow one a new note. The legend on the left edge opens and closes at any time.",
  "tourMapLayersTitle": "What the map shows",
  "tourMapLayersText": "The top button: which trails the map shows, the official trails of the region, and places such as food stops, water and bike service.",
  "tourMapLayersSheetTitle": "Choose places and official trails",
  "tourMapLayersSheetText": "Official trails and way quality on or off, places by group. What is off here stays off until you turn it back on.",
  "tourMapOfflineTitle": "Maps without signal",
  "tourMapOfflineText": "The button below puts the map on your device — for out on the trail, where there is no signal.",
  "tourMapRailTitle": "The toolbar",
  "tourMapRailText": "Here you draw an area the app saves for the trail, or take one away; “My areas” manages them.",
  "tourMapPositionTitle": "To you and to us",
  "tourMapPositionText": "The position button brings the map to you — your location never leaves the device. Top right, the light bulb: report an idea or a bug; it becomes a public entry on GitHub.",
  "tourMapRecordTitle": "Record a ride",
  "tourMapRecordText": "The big button records a ride — door to door, only on your device, even without signal. Afterwards you split it into trails; only those go to your buddies.",
  "coachLater": "Later",
  "coachNotNow": "Not now",
  "coachNext": "Next",
  "coachShowMe": "Show me",
  "coachTargetLost": "What this step points at is not visible right now. “Next” moves on.",
  "coachPosition": "{position} of {count}",
  "coachSkip": "Skip",
  "coachDone": "Let's go",
  "tourSplitIntroTitle": "Split your first ride",
  "tourSplitIntroText": "The ride becomes trails: the app recognizes known ones and suggests new ones. Only the pieces you choose go to your buddies — never the whole ride.",
  "tourSplitKnownTitle": "Already known",
  "tourSplitKnownText": "Trails that you or your buddies already have are recognized by their line. They come pre-ticked and go out as a confirmation — that keeps the trail current.",
  "tourSplitTakeOverTitle": "Now yours",
  "tourSplitTakeOverText": "You are riding one of your buddies’ trails for the first time: name, grade and character are prefilled from your network. With your stars it becomes yours — without a rating the piece does not go out.",
  "tourSplitQuestionTitle": "Still true?",
  "tourSplitQuestionText": "Something was reported on this trail that nobody has confirmed yet. You were just there — one tap answers it, with the time of your ride.",
  "tourSplitCandidateTitle": "A candidate",
  "tourSplitCandidateText": "A piece that could be a new trail: a descent off the known ways, or marked on the go. Set start and end with the handles, the map follows along; name, grade and character go right here.",
  "tourSplitHomeTitle": "Close to home",
  "tourSplitHomeText": "If a piece starts or ends near the start or finish of your ride, the app tells you — a ride often starts at your front door, and a trail should not give it away. Move the handle away if needed.",
  "tourSplitNoRoadsTitle": "Save an area first",
  "tourSplitNoRoadsText": "The app only finds new pieces where it knows the ways — from a saved area. Save one over the ride (layers button on the map), then split it again from “My rides”.",
  "tourSplitPickTitle": "What the search misses",
  "tourSplitPickText": "A jump line, a flat flow trail? This puts a candidate over the whole ride; the handles do the rest.",
  "tourSplitSubmitTitle": "What goes to buddies",
  "tourSplitSubmitText": "Only the ticked pieces go out, as trails to your buddies. The ride itself stays on your device, under “My rides”.",
  "tourTrailsIntroTitle": "Your trails",
  "tourTrailsIntroChainTitle": "On to the trails?",
  "tourTrailsIntroText": "All trails of your network as a list: what you have ridden and what your buddies contribute. Here you find a trail faster than on the map.",
  "tourTrailsRowTitle": "Reading a row",
  "tourTrailsRowText": "Stripe and sign carry the difficulty; the word says whose trail it is — MINE or your buddies’ names. A tap opens the sheet.",
  "tourTrailsSheetTitle": "Numbers and profile",
  "tourTrailsSheetText": "Length, elevation, grade and the elevation profile below. A tap on the grade shows all ratings — and what S0 to S5 mean.",
  "tourTrailsGradeTitle": "Your rating",
  "tourTrailsGradeText": "Tap your own S grade and your stars here. What is shown is what your network says — not just you.",
  "tourTrailsContributionTitle": "What you contribute",
  "tourTrailsContributionText": "Name, character, rating, visibility, description and link — your contribution to the trail. “Only me” keeps it hidden from buddies.",
  "tourTrailsNoteTitle": "Tell what is going on",
  "tourTrailsNoteText": "A note says what is going on right now: a fallen tree, new jumps, with a photo if you like. Buddies see it with a yellow edge until they have read it. A closure or the condition is reported next to it.",
  "tourTrailsSearchTitle": "Search and narrow down",
  "tourTrailsSearchText": "Search by name and buddy, typos included; the chips narrow down by map view, S grade range, character or report. Next to them, the sort order. Except for the map view, the filter applies on the map too.",
  "tourTrailsImportTitle": "Bring in a GPX",
  "tourTrailsImportText": "The icon at the top right reads GPX or zip files from other apps. Short and downhill becomes a trail, a whole loop becomes a ride — which you then split into trails.",
  "tourBuddysIntroTitle": "Your buddies",
  "tourBuddysIntroChainTitle": "On to your buddies?",
  "tourBuddysIntroText": "Who sees your trails — and you theirs. Only direct buddies, nothing beyond; there is no public map.",
  "tourBuddysInviteTitle": "Invite someone",
  "tourBuddysInviteText": "Sends a link to TrailBuddy through your messenger app — with your username, so you are found right away.",
  "tourBuddysSearchTitle": "Looking for buddies",
  "tourBuddysSearchText": "Search by username or the exact email address. You see each other’s trails only once the request is accepted.",
  "tourBuddysRequestsTitle": "Open requests",
  "tourBuddysRequestsText": "Requests to you show up here with accept and decline; requests you sent can be withdrawn.",
  "tourBuddysRowTitle": "A buddy in the list",
  "tourBuddysRowText": "“n shared” counts trails you both know. The pencil gives the buddy a name only you see; the speech bubble opens your messages.",
  "tourBuddysConnectTitle": "When you connect",
  "tourBuddysConnectText": "When you connect, identical trails become ONE trail with two names, the rest is added. If you part ways, their trails disappear from your map again.",
  "tourExampleBadge": "Example",
  "tourExampleTrailName": "Example: Beech Slope",
  "tourExampleTrailStats": "1.8 km · ↓ 210 m",
  "tourExampleTrailLength": "1.8 km",
  "tourExampleTrailHint": "This is what a trail looks like once you have imported or recorded one.",
  "tourExampleBuddyName": "Example: Mira",
  "helpIntro": "The essentials in six steps. Everything else you will find by trying it out.",
  "helpImportTitle": "Importing trails",
  "helpImportText": "You bring in GPX or zip files from other apps through the icon at the top right of the “Trails” tab, or in your profile under “Import trails”. A short track that mostly goes downhill becomes a trail; a whole loop is a ride — you split it into trails with the scissors in the import. Only trails go to your buddies, never the whole ride.",
  "helpMapTitle": "Reading the map",
  "helpMapText": "The color of a line is its difficulty, like on a ski slope: green S0, blue S1, red S2, black from S3; a white dashed edge means S4 or S5, gray not rated yet, magenta uphill. The style of the line is its condition: solid means all good, crumbly worn, dashed beaten up, faded barely rideable. An orange edge means a report (closed, destroyed or changed), a yellow one a new note; dashed violet lines are official trails — the legend on the left edge of the map lays all of this out. Every trail starts with its sign, and below it a dot whose arrow shows the riding direction. A tap on the sign or on the line selects the trail — a small card appears at the bottom, a tap on it opens the sheet. A long press on the map offers “Route from here” and “Route to here”.",
  "helpRideTitle": "Recording and splitting a ride",
  "helpRideText": "In the Android app, the big button at the bottom right of the map records a ride — even without signal, and it stays on your device. On the way you mark with the flag where a trail starts and ends. Afterwards you split the ride: the app recognizes known trails, and you pick new pieces yourself. Exported as GPX, the ride loads into any other app. Before you go, you plan a loop with the loop button: tap trails (tap again to remove), parameters, list and area on the left, then compute — offline, from your saved areas; the loop then sits under “My rides”. “Navigate” shows it on the way: the map turns with you, the rest of the route and your distance to it are at the top, and “Back to the route” next to them leads you back; with the app in the background both are in the notification, and swiped home the map stays as a small window. In “My rides” a finished navigation continues at the top; every ride shows its bike — a tap switches it; swipe left to delete, a long press selects several. The web app has no recording.",
  "helpBuddysTitle": "Buddies and visibility",
  "helpBuddysText": "You see your trails and those of your direct buddies — nobody else’s; there is no public map. You find buddies in the “Buddies” tab by username or exact email. If two recordings are the same way, they become ONE trail, even with two names. What you set to “Only me” nobody else sees.",
  "helpContributionTitle": "Your contribution to a trail",
  "helpContributionText": "In the sheet of a trail you contributed yourself, you enter name, S grade, character, stars, visibility, description and a link under “My contribution”. “Report” says what applies right now — the {report} status (closed, destroyed, changed) and the condition; it is confirmed when you rode the trail or are on site. A note tells buddies what is going on and lights up yellow for them. The navigation icon at the top of the sheet hands the start of the trail to your navigation app; “To trail head” computes the way there itself — offline, from your saved areas, with elevation and time.",
  "helpOfflineTitle": "Without signal",
  "helpOfflineText": "The app shows your trails offline too, as of your last download. What you contribute or report without signal waits in the outbox and goes out as soon as you have signal again. For the map to show anything, save an area beforehand: the “Offline maps” button on the map, then draw; manage them under “My areas” in your profile — ideally at home on Wi-Fi.",
  "helpMapTour": "Show the tour on the map",
  "helpTabTour": "Tour: {tab}",
  "helpSplitTour": "Tour: splitting a ride",
  "helpSplitTourHint": "Record a ride first — the big button on the map. Then the tour uses it to show how a ride turns into trails.",
  "helpDiscover": "Discover features and tips",
  "safetyNoteTitle": "Safety note",
  "safetyNoteDialogTitle": "Before you start",
  "safetyNoteConfirm": "Got it",
  "safetyNote": "You ride at your own risk. TrailBuddy shows what you and your buddies have ridden — it does not tell you whether a way may be ridden or is safe right now. Respect closures, trail rules and nature protection on site. A buddy’s report is no clearance, and no report does not mean everything is open.",
  "discoverTitle": "Discover",
  "discoverLead": "What TrailBuddy can do — including what is easy to miss while using it. “Show me” gives a short demo, “Try it” takes you straight there.",
  "discoverBadgeTip": "Tip",
  "discoverBadgeNew": "New",
  "discoverTry": "Try it",
  "discoverShowMe": "Show me",
  "highlightSheetRecapTitle": "What TrailBuddy can do by now",
  "highlightSheetNewTitle": "New in TrailBuddy",
  "highlightSheetMore": "{count, plural, =1{Discover 1 more} other{Discover {count} more}}",
  "highlightSheetAll": "All features and tips",
  "highlightSheetChangelog": "All changes",
  "highlightNavMinimizeTitle": "Minimise",
  "highlightNavMinimizeText": "While navigating, “Minimise” puts the map straight into the small window — with the next section below. The notification gives it in two lines: how far and how high to the trail head, on the trail what is left.",
  "highlightNavTrailEndTitle": "Trail done",
  "highlightNavTrailEndText": "At the end of a trail while navigating: your time on it, the metres of descent, your top speed — and a tip on how it was today. Your buddies see that as its condition.",
  "highlightNavSectionsTitle": "Navigation from trail to trail",
  "highlightNavSectionsText": "While navigating, the map counts down to the next trail head: km, elevation, the steep ramp. At the head you see the grade, the condition and your buddy’s note; at the bottom the whole loop as a band.",
  "highlightNotePhotosTitle": "A photo with your note",
  "highlightNotePhotosText": "The tree across the trail, the new ramp: you can now attach a photo to a note. The same buddies who see the note see it, for 90 days — without location data in the image.",
  "highlightMessagesTitle": "Messages to your buddies",
  "highlightMessagesText": "The speech bubble next to a buddy opens your messages — up to three already while a request is open. With notifications on, a reply arrives even when the app is closed.",
  "highlightWholeRegionTitle": "The whole region offline",
  "highlightWholeRegionText": "In “My areas” you save the whole map of a region on your phone, with places, heights and ways. What your areas already have is not fetched again; “Update” later fetches only what is out of date.",
  "highlightContoursTitle": "Contour lines",
  "highlightContoursText": "Under “Map layers” you can add contour lines — subtle beneath ways and trails, labelled about every 100 m. They come from the terrain model, in saved areas even without reception.",
  "highlightNavPipTitle": "Navigation in a small window",
  "highlightNavPipText": "If you swipe home while navigating — or tap “Minimise” —, the map stays as a small window above the other apps, with the next section below. “Stop” works right in the window.",
  "highlightNavNoticeTitle": "Navigation in the notification",
  "highlightNavNoticeText": "Phone in your pocket or another app in front: the notification shows the next section — how far and how high to the trail head, on the trail what is left — and whether you are on the route. “Stop navigation” works right there.",
  "highlightNavRejoinTitle": "Back to the route",
  "highlightNavRejoinText": "Off the route while navigating: one tap shows the way back, 200 m ahead instead of to the nearest point. A navigation you stopped continues at the top of “My rides”.",
  "highlightNavigationTitle": "Navigate",
  "highlightNavigationText": "In the result of a loop or a route, and for every ride in “My rides”: the map turns with you, at the top you see what is left, the elevation and the distance to the route — without turn instructions.",
  "highlightRouteViasTitle": "Drag the route by hand",
  "highlightRouteViasText": "Tap the line of a planned loop or of a route to a trail: a via point sits there that you can drag, and the route runs through it. A tap on the point removes it again.",
  "highlightWayQualityTitle": "How good is the way?",
  "highlightWayQualityText": "From zoom level 13 the map shows how good a forest road is and how hard a path: solid for good or easy, dashed for medium, dotted for poor or hard. The data comes from OpenStreetMap; you can turn it off under “Map layers”.",
  "highlightRouteElevationTitle": "Elevation profile of the loop",
  "highlightRouteElevationText": "Below the totals of a planned loop you now see its elevation profile, compact over the whole distance — the same for the route to a trail. The heights come from the terrain model of your areas.",
  "highlightPlacePlanTitle": "A place as start or finish",
  "highlightPlacePlanText": "Tap a place on the map, such as a car park or a fountain: “Start in planner” and “Finish in planner” make it the start or finish. While the planner waits for its start, a tap on a place takes exactly its position.",
  "highlightOnePlannerTitle": "One planner for every way",
  "highlightOnePlannerText": "“To the trail head”, the navigation icon, “Route to here” and “Route here” now all open the planner and compute right away. Back takes you to the normal map in one step, and after navigating the result is there again.",
  "highlightRouteEasyTitle": "An easy way to the trail head",
  "highlightRouteEasyText": "Besides “Direct” and “Fun”, “To the trail head” and “Route here” now offer “Easy”: cycleways and quiet roads first, as little climbing as possible. Save your legs for the trail.",
  "highlightTrailHeadPlanTitle": "Start or finish at a trail head",
  "highlightTrailHeadPlanText": "In a trail's sheet, “Start in planner” and “Finish in planner” open the planner with the trail head as start or finish. As a start, the trail is picked right away.",
  "highlightLoopEndTitle": "Loop, last trail or a finish",
  "highlightLoopEndText": "In the planner you now choose where the ride ends: back at the start, at the end of the last trail, or at a finish you tap on the map. Start and end each carry their flag.",
  "highlightRouteProfileScrubTitle": "Walk along the elevation profile",
  "highlightRouteProfileScrubText": "Tap the elevation profile of a planned loop or route, or slide your finger across it: a bike shows you the spot on the map while the whole route stays in view. The profile now has a km scale too.",
  "highlightRidesTidyTitle": "Tidy up My rides",
  "highlightRidesTidyText": "Every ride shows its bike, a tap switches it. Swipe left to delete, a long press selects several. On GPX import the app suggests the bike from the climbing rate.",
  "highlightTrailListFiltersTitle": "Filter by map view and S grade",
  "highlightTrailListFiltersText": "“On the map” shows only the trails in the current map view in the list. You set the S grade as a range, such as “S3 and up” or “S1–S3”.",
  "highlightRideImportTitle": "Old rides count too",
  "highlightRideImportText": "Bring rides from other apps into “My rides” by GPX import — with the bike you rode them on. The rider profile then also learns from them how fast you climb.",
  "highlightRoutePrefsTitle": "Ways to your taste",
  "highlightRoutePrefsText": "Roads, hiking trails uphill, steep ramps: in the planner settings you say for each whether you avoid them or don’t mind them. That applies to loops and to the route to a trail.",
  "highlightSteepClimbsTitle": "Avoid steep ramps",
  "highlightSteepClimbsText": "Loops and routes to a trail avoid very steep climbs where a flatter way exists — the steeper, the more, on gravel and paths more than on tarmac. Uphill trails stay wanted.",
  "highlightTerrainHeightsTitle": "Heights from the terrain model",
  "highlightTerrainHeightsText": "If a trail has no heights, the sheet shows its profile from the terrain model — labelled and never saved. The import checks a file’s heights and offers to discard bad ones.",
  "highlightOnlineFillTitle": "Loops without an area",
  "highlightOnlineFillText": "With reception the planner fetches the ways your areas lack from the map host — so a loop works even without a saved area. You can turn it off under Settings.",
  "highlightMapLegendTitle": "The legend on the map",
  "highlightMapLegendText": "On the left edge sits a narrow tab with the run colours. A tap opens the legend — colours, line styles, edges —, a second one closes it. The app remembers how you like it.",
  "highlightMapLayersTitle": "Layers in one tap",
  "highlightMapLayersText": "The top button on the right opens the map layers directly: trail filter, official trails and places in one sheet. Offline maps have their own button below, and the light bulb now sits at the top right.",
  "highlightMapSelectTitle": "Tap a trail, route from here",
  "highlightMapSelectText": "A tap highlights a trail and shows a small card at the bottom; a second one opens its sheet. A long press on the map offers “Route from here” and “Route to here”.",
  "highlightTrailNavTitle": "Navigate to the trail",
  "highlightTrailNavText": "The navigation icon on every trail: with your navigation app, or in TrailBuddy, direct or fun — then the route takes in trails. It remembers what you usually want.",
  "highlightLoopPlannerTitle": "Plan a loop",
  "highlightLoopPlannerText": "The loop button opens the planner: tap trails, on the left start, settings, list and area — the app links them downhill over the ways of your areas, offline. As a planned ride or GPX.",
  "highlightGpxExportTitle": "Trails and rides as GPX",
  "highlightGpxExportText": "Every trail and every ride can be passed on as a GPX file — to Komoot, Garmin, a navigation app or as a backup. Trails in the sheet, rides under “My rides”.",
  "highlightTrailHeadTitle": "To the trail head, offline",
  "highlightTrailHeadText": "“To trail head” in the sheet works out the way from your position to the start of the trail — from your saved areas, without a network: line on the map, elevation, time, and whether a hiking trail is part of it.",
  "highlightNavigateTitle": "Getting to the trail",
  "highlightNavigateText": "The navigation icon at the top of the sheet hands the start of the trail to your navigation app — you pick which one. Without a navigation app the coordinates go to the clipboard.",
  "highlightTrailEndsTitle": "Start and direction",
  "highlightTrailEndsText": "Every trail has a dot with an arrow at its start, in its colour. So you see on the map where it begins and which way it runs.",
  "highlightKurzanleitungTitle": "The quick guide",
  "highlightKurzanleitungText": "The essentials in six steps, with the real icons — and from there you can start every tour again.",
  "highlightStillValidTitle": "Still valid?",
  "highlightStillValidText": "If your reports and conditions are older than 30 days, the profile asks: Yes, No or Don’t know — and again in 14 days.",
  "highlightMarksTitle": "Trail starts, trail ends",
  "highlightMarksText": "During a recording a flag sits above the record button. Tap it at the start and at the end of a trail — in the split sheet that section is then already ticked.",
  "highlightTakeoverTitle": "Make a buddy’s trail yours",
  "highlightTakeoverText": "When you ride one of your buddies’ trails for the first time, you take it over in the split sheet with your stars. Then it stays yours, even if the buddy deletes their contribution.",
  "highlightReportsTitle": "Report what applies now",
  "highlightReportsText": "“Report” in the sheet says whether a trail is closed, destroyed or changed, and what it looks like right now — from barely rideable to well kept. It counts as confirmed when you rode it or are on site.",
  "highlightRatingTitle": "Stars for trails",
  "highlightRatingText": "Trails you have ridden get one to five stars from you. The list can sort by them.",
  "highlightGradeColorsTitle": "Colour means difficulty",
  "highlightGradeColorsText": "Like on the slopes: green S0, blue S1, red S2, black from S3. The style of the line tells the condition, a dashed edge S4 or S5.",
  "highlightConnectMergeTitle": "Connecting means merging",
  "highlightConnectMergeText": "When you accept a request, identical trails become ONE trail with two names. The card afterwards tells you what you share and what is new.",
  "highlightImportSplitTitle": "A ride becomes trails",
  "highlightImportSplitText": "Split a whole loop with the scissors: the app recognizes known trails and suggests new ones. Only the pieces you choose go to your buddies.",
  "highlightOfflineAreasTitle": "Maps for the road",
  "highlightOfflineAreasText": "Under “Offline maps” you draw an area that the app saves — then the map is there even without reception. “My areas” in the profile manages them.",
  "highlightRideRecordTitle": "Record a ride",
  "highlightRideRecordText": "In the Android app the big button records your ride, even without reception. It stays on your device until you split it.",
  "highlightOfficialTrailsTitle": "Official trails",
  "highlightOfficialTrailsText": "Singletrails designated by the region, dashed in violet — with status and source. Turn them on and off under “Map layers”.",
  "highlightTrailNotesTitle": "Notes for buddies",
  "highlightTrailNotesText": "“Tree down”: a note in the sheet tells your buddies what is going on. For them the trail glows yellow until they have read it.",
  "highlightMergeProposalsTitle": "Are these the same?",
  "highlightMergeProposalsText": "If a buddy takes your trail for another one, or two lie almost on top of each other, the app asks: the same, different, or view both on the map.",
  "highlightTrailMergeTitle": "Merge duplicate trails",
  "highlightTrailMergeText": "If a trail lies just next to another — say after a GPX import —, the sheet shows “Is a duplicate …”. Your recordings move to the one that stays.",
  "highlightToursTitle": "Watch the tours again",
  "highlightToursText": "Map, trails, buddies and splitting a ride explain themselves in short tours. To restart: Profile → Quick guide.",
  "highlightPickSectionTitle": "Pick a section yourself",
  "highlightPickSectionText": "If the search in the split sheet misses a jump line, “Pick a section yourself” lays a candidate over the whole ride — the handles do the rest.",
  "highlightTrailLinkTitle": "A link to the source",
  "highlightTrailLinkText": "In “My contribution” a trail can point to a page, such as the club’s. The sheet names the address; it opens in the browser.",
  "highlightPlannedTitle": "Planned or ridden",
  "highlightPlannedText": "A GPX file without ride times counts as only planned. If you rode it, enter “Ridden on …” when importing.",
  "highlightTraitsTitle": "A trail’s character",
  "highlightTraitsText": "Flowy, jump line, rocky, steep, uphill: the two most frequent ones sit on the sign — and the filters “Flowy” and “Jumps” search for them.",
  "highlightGradeVotesTitle": "Who rated it how",
  "highlightGradeVotesText": "A tap on the S grade in the sheet shows every rating in your network — and what S0 to S5 mean.",
  "highlightVisibilityTitle": "Only for me",
  "highlightVisibilityText": "In “My contribution” you keep a trail hidden from your buddies. It stays on your map.",
  "highlightPoisTitle": "Places on the map",
  "highlightPoisText": "Food stops, water, bike service: which places the map shows you choose under “Map layers”, the top button on the right.",
  "highlightMyPositionTitle": "Where am I?",
  "highlightMyPositionText": "The position button brings the map to you. Your location never leaves the device.",
  "highlightBuddyAliasTitle": "Your own name for buddies",
  "highlightBuddyAliasText": "The pencil next to a buddy gives them a name only you see — everywhere in the app.",
  "highlightInviteTitle": "Invite buddies",
  "highlightInviteText": "Top right in the “Buddies” tab: a link to TrailBuddy with your username, so people find you right away.",
  "highlightNotificationsTitle": "Notifications",
  "highlightNotificationsText": "When a buddy reports a trail or writes a note, your phone tells you — turn it on in the profile.",
  "highlightRiderLearnTitle": "Learned from your rides",
  "highlightRiderLearnText": "Under “Rider profile”: “Learn from my rides” reads time and GPS height of your recordings and tunes climbing rate and flat speed per profile to you. You can reset it at any time.",
  "highlightRiderProfileTitle": "Bike or e-bike",
  "highlightRiderProfileText": "Under “Rider profile” in the profile: how fast you climb, how costly a hiking trail is, how much elevation a loop may have. Route planning works with it; every ride remembers it.",
  "highlightAppearanceTitle": "Light or dark",
  "highlightAppearanceText": "Under “Appearance” in the profile — or like the system. The map stays light; it reads better in the sun.",
  "demoOpenTrailFirstTitle": "Open a trail",
  "demoOpenTrailFirstText": "A tap on the row opens the sheet — the same as on the map.",
  "demoNoTrailYetTitle": "Get a trail first",
  "demoNoTrailYetText": "This works on a trail. Get one by GPX from another app, record a ride or connect with buddies.",
  "demoNoOwnTrailTitle": "On your own trails",
  "demoNoOwnTrailText": "This works on trails you contributed yourself — by GPX or from a recorded ride. You make a buddy’s trail yours the first time you ride it.",
  "demoAndroidOnlyTitle": "In the Android app",
  "demoAndroidOnlyText": "Recording happens in the Android app — a browser gets no positions in the background.",
  "demoFindBuddyFirstTitle": "Find a buddy first",
  "demoFindBuddyFirstText": "This works with your buddies. Search here for a username or an exact email address — or invite someone.",
  "demoWholeRegionTitle": "In “My areas”",
  "demoWholeRegionText": "There each region has “save whole region” — on the phone, with the size shown first. Above it, a line per region counts how many tiles are older than the current state.",
  "demoOnlineFill1Title": "Ways from the map host",
  "demoOnlineFill1Text": "The planner works over the ways of your areas. With reception it fetches what is missing from the map host — at most {tiles} tiles per plan, only for this session.",
  "demoOnlineFill2Title": "Check offline",
  "demoOnlineFill2Text": "Under Settings you turn off “Fill in missing paths online” — then it plans as if in a dead zone, and you see at home whether your areas are enough for the loop.",
  "demoContoursTitle": "Lines of equal height",
  "demoContoursText": "Turn them on here. The closer they lie, the steeper — the interval adapts to the terrain, and the legend names it.",
  "demoWayQuality1Title": "The quality of the ways",
  "demoWayQuality1Text": "Turn it off and on again here. It comes from OpenStreetMap — where nothing is recorded there, the way stays as the map draws it.",
  "demoWayQuality2Title": "What the strokes mean",
  "demoWayQuality2Text": "Under “Forest road” and “Path” the legend shows which stroke means what. The more broken, the rougher.",
  "demoMapSelect1Title": "Select first",
  "demoMapSelect1Text": "A tap on a trail highlights it, and a small card with a navigation icon appears at the bottom. A tap on it — or a second one on the trail — opens the sheet; a tap beside it deselects.",
  "demoMapSelect2Title": "Long press on the map",
  "demoMapSelect2Text": "Hold your finger on a spot and the map offers “Route from here” (a loop with this start), “Route to here” (the way from your position) and your navigation app.",
  "demoTrailNavTitle": "The navigation icon",
  "demoTrailNavText": "With your navigation app, or in TrailBuddy: direct, or fun — then the route takes in descents. Once saved as the default, only a long press asks again.",
  "demoNavMinimizeTitle": "Minimise",
  "demoNavMinimizeText": "Plan a loop and navigate: at the bottom next to “Screen”, “Minimise” puts the map into the small window, with the next section below. A tap on the window brings TrailBuddy back.",
  "demoNavTrailEndTitle": "Trail done",
  "demoNavTrailEndText": "Navigate a loop over trails: at the end of each trail you see time, metres of descent and top speed. One tap tells your buddies how it was today — “Continue” shows the next section.",
  "demoNavSectionsTitle": "From trail to trail",
  "demoNavSectionsText": "Plan a loop and tap “Navigate”: at the top you see how far and how much climbing it is to the next trail head; at the head the grade, the condition and your buddy’s note. At the bottom the loop as a band.",
  "demoNavPipTitle": "Navigation in a small window",
  "demoNavPipText": "Navigate a loop or a route to a trail and swipe home: the map stays as a small window above the other apps, and a tap on it brings TrailBuddy back.",
  "demoNavNoticeTitle": "Navigation in the notification",
  "demoNavNoticeText": "Navigate a loop or a route to a trail and switch to another app: at the top, the notification shows what is left, the elevation and whether you are on the route — updated every five seconds.",
  "demoNavRejoinTitle": "Back to the route",
  "demoNavRejoinText": "Navigate a loop or a route to a trail. If you are more than 30 m off, “Back to the route” appears at the bottom: the way there is then drawn dashed ahead of the route.",
  "demoNavigationTitle": "Navigate from the result",
  "demoNavigationText": "Plan a loop or a route to a trail, then “Navigate”: the map turns with your direction, at the top you see what is left, the elevation and the distance to the route. Planned rides start from the ride’s menu.",
  "demoRouteViasTitle": "Via points in the result",
  "demoRouteViasText": "Plan a loop or a route to a trail. A tap on the line sets a point; drag it to where the route should go. For a loop the order of the trails stays as it is.",
  "demoRouteElevationTitle": "The profile in the result",
  "demoRouteElevationText": "Plan a loop or a route to a trail: below the totals you see the elevation profile, from start to finish. If a piece has no height, it is left out — nothing is made up.",
  "demoPlacePlanTitle": "Plan from the car park",
  "demoPlacePlanText": "Turn on the places you need here. A place's sheet then has “Start in planner” and “Finish in planner”.",
  "demoOnePlannerTitle": "To the trail head, in the planner",
  "demoOnePlannerText": "The button opens the planner with the trail head as finish and computes at once: Direct, Easy or Fun, with draggable points, “Navigate” and “Directions”. Back, and you are on the map again.",
  "demoRouteEasyTitle": "An easy way to the trail head",
  "demoRouteEasyText": "“To the trail head” shows the way on the map; at the top of the sheet pick “Easy” — then it runs over cycleways and quiet roads, with as little climbing as possible.",
  "demoTrailHeadPlanTitle": "Plan from the trail head",
  "demoTrailHeadPlanText": "“Start in planner” opens the planner with the trail head as start and this trail picked; “Finish in planner” ends the route at the trail head.",
  "demoLoopEnd1Title": "Not every ride is a loop",
  "demoLoopEnd1Text": "Open the planner and pick your trails as usual.",
  "demoLoopEnd2Title": "Where does the ride end?",
  "demoLoopEnd2Text": "In the parameters: Loop, Last trail or To a point. For a point, tap it on the map; the bar gets its own button for it.",
  "demoRouteProfileScrubTitle": "Where is that climb?",
  "demoRouteProfileScrubText": "Plan a loop or a route to a trail and slide your finger across the elevation profile: the bike on the map follows, with distance and height of the spot above the profile.",
  "demoLoopPlanner1Title": "A loop from your trails",
  "demoLoopPlanner1Text": "The button opens the planner: a rail of its own on the left, and every trail you tap on the map joins the loop — a second tap takes it out again.",
  "demoLoopPlanner2Title": "The planner’s rail",
  "demoLoopPlanner2Text": "At the top the start (your position or a tapped spot) and the settings — time, elevation, hiking trails, radius. Below, the list and the area: draw round it, and the trails inside are in. At the very bottom: plan.",
  "demoTrailListFiltersTitle": "Map view and S grade",
  "demoTrailListFiltersText": "“On the map” keeps only the trails in the map view — the list follows when you move the map. The S grade chip opens two sliders for the range. It applies on the map too.",
  "demoRideImportTitle": "Rides from other apps",
  "demoRideImportText": "Here TrailBuddy reads GPX or zip files. In the Android app, “Rides for your rider profile” then appears below the tracks: choose the bike, save, let it learn. The rides stay on the device.",
  "demoRoutePrefsTitle": "Avoid or don’t mind",
  "demoRoutePrefsText": "In the planner under “Settings”: roads, hiking trails uphill and steep ramps, each avoid or don’t mind. Don’t mind is not free — a fraction of the penalty remains. The device remembers your choice, and it applies to the route to a trail too.",
  "demoSteepClimbsTitle": "Flatter where possible",
  "demoSteepClimbsText": "The planner and “To trail head” count every metre of climbing above 10 % gradient extra, and the steeper, the more — on gravel and paths three times as much as on tarmac. A detour that climbs more gently then wins. Uphill trails never count as too steep.",
  "demoTerrainHeightsTitle": "Heights without a recording",
  "demoTerrainHeightsText": "If no contribution has heights, they come from the terrain model (90 m): with reception from the map host, otherwise from your areas. The tile then carries a “≈”, the profile says so — nothing is saved.",
  "demoGpxExportTitle": "The line as a file",
  "demoGpxExportText": "Passes the trail on as a GPX file — through the share menu to any app that reads GPX. Only the line with its name; no buddies, no notes. Rides are exported under “My rides”.",
  "demoTrailHeadTitle": "The way from your areas",
  "demoTrailHeadText": "Works out the way from your position to the start of the trail — offline, from the ways in your saved areas, according to your rider profile. The map shows the line, the sheet elevation and time; as GPX it goes to any navigation app.",
  "demoNavigateTitle": "To your navigation app",
  "demoNavigateText": "Hands the start of the trail to your navigation app — you choose which one. The app itself makes no connection for this; without a navigation app the coordinates go to the clipboard.",
  "demoTrailEnds1Title": "Where it begins",
  "demoTrailEnds1Text": "The dot at the start points its arrow in the riding direction, in the trail’s colour, from the zoom level of the signs.",
  "demoTrailEnds2Title": "Get a trail first",
  "demoTrailEnds2Text": "The map shows this on a trail. Get one by GPX from another app, record a ride or connect with buddies.",
  "demoKurzanleitungTitle": "Here it is",
  "demoKurzanleitungText": "Six sections with the real icons, plus the buttons for every tour.",
  "demoStillValid1Title": "Check your entries",
  "demoStillValid1Text": "The number says how many of your reports and conditions are older than 30 days. One tap, then for each trail Yes, No or Don’t know.",
  "demoStillValid2Title": "Nothing to check right now",
  "demoStillValid2Text": "Once one of your entries is older than 30 days, “Still valid?” appears here in the profile with the number.",
  "demoMarksTitle": "The flag comes with the ride",
  "demoMarksText": "While a recording runs, a flag sits above this button: tap it at the start of a trail, and again at the end.",
  "demoTakeoverTitle": "On the first ride",
  "demoTakeoverText": "When you ride one of your buddies’ trails, its row in the split sheet opens up: prefilled from the network. With your stars it becomes yours. For trails you already have, the sheet offers “Take over”.",
  "demoReportsTitle": "Report here",
  "demoReportsText": "Closed, destroyed, changed — and the condition. It counts as confirmed when you rode it or are on site; otherwise it shows as “to be confirmed”.",
  "demoConnectMerge1Title": "Accept a request",
  "demoConnectMerge1Text": "When you accept, identical trails become ONE trail with two names. Afterwards this shows what you share and what is new.",
  "demoConnectMerge2Title": "A request first",
  "demoConnectMerge2Text": "Search for a buddy by username or exact email and send a request. As soon as they accept, the app merges your trails.",
  "demoMergeProposals1Title": "Check pairs",
  "demoMergeProposals1Text": "The number says how many trail pairs might be one. One tap, then for each pair: the same, different, or view both on the map.",
  "demoMergeProposals2Title": "No pair right now",
  "demoMergeProposals2Text": "If a buddy takes one of your trails for another, or two lie almost on top of each other, “Are these the same?” appears here in the profile with the number — and the same question in the trail’s sheet.",
  "demoTrailMergeTitle": "Two lines, one trail",
  "demoTrailMergeText": "If another trail lies roughly alongside, “Is a duplicate …” appears below the export. You choose which one stays; your recordings, your contribution and your notes move there. “Separate” undoes it.",
  "demoToursTitle": "Watch again",
  "demoToursText": "Here you restart the tours for trails and buddies; below, the tour for splitting a ride.",
  "demoRidesTidyTitle": "In “My rides”",
  "demoRidesTidyText": "Every ride shows whether it was ridden on a bike or an e-bike — a tap switches it, and the rider profile then learns correctly. Swipe left to delete, a long press selects several.",
  "demoPickSectionTitle": "Via “My rides”",
  "demoPickSectionText": "The scissors next to a ride open the split sheet; below the candidates you find “Pick a section yourself”.",
  "demoGradeVotesTitle": "A tap on the grade",
  "demoGradeVotesText": "The tile shows your network’s median; a tap on it lists every rating and explains the scale.",
  "demoMessages1Title": "To the conversation",
  "demoMessages1Text": "The speech bubble next to a buddy opens your messages. A number on it means something is unread.",
  "demoMessages2Title": "Start writing",
  "demoMessages2Text": "Up to 500 characters. With notifications on, a reply arrives even when the app is closed; messages disappear again after 30 days.",
  "demoNotificationsTitle": "Turn them on here",
  "demoNotificationsText": "The switch tells you what really gets through — including when the browser or Android does not allow notifications.",
  "demoRiderLearnTitle": "Tuned to you",
  "demoRiderLearnText": "Under “Rider profile” the app learns from your recordings how fast you really climb — per profile, only from your rides, only on this device. The planners then work with it.",
  "demoRiderProfileTitle": "Bike or e-bike",
  "demoRiderProfileText": "The profile changes how fast you climb, how costly a hiking trail uphill is and how much elevation a loop may have. Every ride remembers it at the start.",
  "demoAppearanceTitle": "Light, dark or like the system",
  "demoAppearanceText": "Applies to the app; the map stays light — it reads better in the sun.",
  "areasTitle": "My areas",
